+\subsection{Dimension-specific bounded-minor certificate}
+For $h\in\{45,47\}$ set
+\[
+ Z=3h-7,\quad B_0=(4h-2)Z+27(h+1),\quad
+ D=3(h+1)(h-1)^2,\quad B=2(h-1)B_0.
+\]
+The displayed single-projector numerator is bounded by $B_0$: its four
+terms are bounded by $2Z$, $24(h+1)$, $4(h-1)Z$, and $3(h+1)$.
+Each denominator is $3(h+1)d$ with integer $d\le h-1$, including a source
+line with $d=2$. Two such denominators have least common multiple at most
+$D$, with each multiplier at most $h-1$, giving numerator bound $B$.
+Single frames and complements obey the same conservative bounds.
+
+For correction rank at most $r$, every square minor, multiplied by its
+actual common denominator to power $r$, is an integer of absolute value
+at most
+\[
+ \mathcal B(h,r,D,B)=\sum_{j=0}^r\binom hjj!B^jD^{r-j}.
+\]
+Indeed more than $r$ correction columns vanish; mask columns force their
+rows and a $j$-square correction determinant is bounded by $j!B^j$.
+At $h=47$, the bounds for $r=2,3,4$ are respectively
+\[
+12615104475495936,\quad1369463492120322994642944,\quad
+145362180906936349127921501208576;
+\]
+the $h=45$ bounds are smaller and recorded exactly in the certificate.
+Use primes $p_1=2^{61}-1,p_2=2^{31}-1,p_3=2^{19}-1$; Lucas--Lehmer checks
+prove primality. All constituent denominators are below $p_3$.
+The rank2 bound is below $p_1$; the rank3/4 bounds are below
+$p_1p_2p_3=2596143476298333157846630848266239$.
+Thus zeros as well as nonzeros of every minor are exact: for rank2 use
+$p_1$, and for source growth and core2-to-core1 use all three primes.
+Each northeast corner's rational rank is the maximum of its modular ranks,
+which fixes the lower-lower pivot positions. Consecutive increasing row and
+column pivots are one contiguous child, without gathering or reversal.
